      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was officially incorporated in 1950, giving it a suburban feel that still defines its residential neighborhoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/ohio_harbor-hills",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office operated in Harbor Hills from 1927 until 1943, marking the town’s early 20th‑century growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harbor_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Buckeye Lake’s water, originally part of the Ohio and Erie Canal project, is now mainly used for recreation, offering boating and fishing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harbor_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Harbor Hills borders the village of Buckeye Lake to the west and Thornport to the south, placing it in the heart of Licking County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
